  "count": 2,
  "rationale": "Deploy mfa:admin and mfa:dbadmin. The only way onto db, fileserver or backup is auth_*. It needs either NOT mfa_dbadmin, or admin_dc or admin_adfs. mfa_dbadmin removes the first option. mfa_admin blocks auth_dc and auth_adfs, which are the only routes to foothold_dc and foothold_adfs. So admin_dc and admin_adfs can never be reached. With no foothold on db, fileserver or backup, no escalate_* or exfiltrate_* step can fire. No single control is enough. With mfa:dbadmin alone: phish, then pivot, then auth_appserver, then kerberoast, then auth_dc, then escalate_dc gives admin_dc and opens auth_db. With mfa:admin alone: escalate_ciserver using stolen_admin, then leak_secrets gives stolen_dbadmin, and auth_db is open. With segmented alone: phish_workstation, then escalate_workstation gives admin_workstation, so pivot_internal still works. mfa:user does not stop auth_* because phishing gives foothold_workstation. No single patch removes every path, since alternate hosts and the stolen_admin bypass remain."
 },
